   "id": "bava_metzia.60b.2",
   "daf": "60b",
   "sentenceId": 1,
   "he": "וְלֹא יָבוֹר אֶת הַגְּרִיסִין, דִּבְרֵי אַבָּא שָׁאוּל. וַחֲכָמִים מַתִּירִין וְכוּ׳. מַאן חֲכָמִים? רַבִּי אַחָא, דְּתַנְיָא: רַבִּי אַחָא מַתִּיר בְּדָבָר הַנִּרְאֶה.",
   "en": "The mishna teaches: «And one may not sift ground beans» to remove the waste and charge a higher price; this is «the statement of Abba Shaul. And the Rabbis permit» doing so. The Gemara comments: «Who» are the «Rabbis» whose opinion is cited in the mishna? It is «Rabbi Aḥa, as it is taught» in a baraita: «Rabbi Aḥa permits» mixing, and sifting, and the like, in the case of «an item» in «which» the change «is obvious.»"
  }
 ],
